&= \frac{256^2 + 1968^2}{256^2} \\
&= \frac{256\cdot 257}{256^2} \\
&= \frac{257}{256}
\end{align*} and $a_4 > 1$.

We claim that $a_n > 1,$ for each positive integer $n.$

First, we show by induction that $a_n \ge 1,$ for each positive integer $n.$ The base case $n = 1$ is true.

To verify the inductive step, suppose the claim is true for some $n \ge 1,$ in which case we have $0 \le a_{n - 1} \le 1$ and $1 \le a_{n - 1} + 1 \le \frac{5}{2} \le 2.$ Then,
\begin{align*}
a_n &= 1 + (a_{n - 1} - 1)^2 \\
&\ge 1 + (-1)^2 \\
&= 2 \ge 1.
\end{align*}  Thus, by induction, $a_n \ge 1,$ for each positive integer $n.$

Since $a_n > 1,$ for each integer $n \ge 4,$ we have $\frac{1}{a_4} < 1,$ $\frac{1}{a_5} < 1,$ $\frac{1}{a_6} < 1,$ and so on, and
\[0 < \frac{1}{a_n} \le \frac{1}{a_4} = \frac{256}{257},\ \text{ for each integer } n \ge 4.\] It follows that
\[0 \le \frac{1}{a_n} \le \frac{1}{a_4},\ \text{ and } \ a_n \le \ \frac{1+256}{256} = \frac{257}{256},\ \text{for each integer } n \ge 4.\] Using the above information, we get
