Find the characteristic polynomial of the given matrix:

$$
\left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
-2 & \frac{19}{10} & 5 \\
\frac{89}{10} & \frac{17}{5} & \frac{7}{10} \\
\frac{3}{5} & \frac{1}{5} & -\frac{19}{5} \\
\end{array}
\right)
$$
The characteristic polynomial $p(x)$ of a matrix $A$ is given by $p(x) = \det(A - xI)$, where $I$ is the identity matrix of the same size as $A$. For the given matrix,

$$
A - xI = \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
-2-x & \frac{19}{10} & 5 \\
\frac{89}{10} & \frac{17}{5}-x & \frac{7}{10} \\
\frac{3}{5} & \frac{1}{5} & -\frac{19}{5}-x \\
\end{array}
\right)
$$

We calculate the determinant:

$$
p(x) = \det \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
-2-x & \frac{19}{10} & 5 \\
\frac{89}{10} & \frac{17}{5}-x & \frac{7}{10} \\
\frac{3}{5} & \frac{1}{5} & -\frac{19}{5}-x \\
\end{array}
\right) \\
= -2(-\frac{19}{5}-x))\det \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
\frac{17}{5}-x & \frac{7}{10} \\
\frac{1}{5} & -\frac{19}{5}-x \\
\end{array}
\right) - \frac{19}{10} \det \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
\frac{89}{10} & \frac{7}{10} \\
\frac{3}{5} & -\frac{19}{5}-x \\
\end{array}
\right) + 5 \det \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
\frac{89}{10} & \frac{17}{5}-x \\
\frac{3}{5} & \frac{1}{5} \\
\end{array}
\right) \\
= \ldots \\

= -x^3-\frac{10 x^2}{5}+\frac{1939 x}{50}+\frac{6}{5}
= -x^3-2 x^2+\frac{1939 x}{50}+\frac{6}{5}
$$

Hence, the characteristic polynomial is $p(x) = -x^3-2 x^2+\frac{1939 x}{50}+\frac{6}{5}$.

